No rush, please take your time, and thank you for your responses.

In this case I made a mistake when copying the cope here to the group, but the example is still valid. I am using viewClade to reduce the tree (cut outgroups) at node 164. I consider the rest my entire tree because that's what I want to plot. The mistake was having number 154 in the scale function. I was supposed to be 164. If you do that you get something similar to your first figure, where the branches don't fit the canvas. You might notice that even though your p2 fits the canvas, the scale function didn't really work, the terminals are still cramped on each other. But I guess this might be impossible to do, so I will try to figure something out some other way.

