that’s quite horrible.

%<+% was designed to attach data to one tree. Your ‘myTreeID’ can’t be recognized.

# #Ugly hack, replacing the tree ".id"
mytreeplot$data[".id"] <- mytreeplot$data["myTreeID"]

This is not a hack. you are trying to mess everything up.

The following code should works for your case:
x= fortify(mytrees)
y = merge(x, mydf, by.x=c("node", "parent", ".id"), by.y=c("node", "parent", "myTreeID"))
ggplot(y, aes(x,y, color=myLength)) + geom_tree()+ theme_tree() +
  facet_wrap(~.id, ncol=4) +
  geom_treescale(offset=1.25) +
  scale_color_continuous(low='darkgreen', high='red', name= 'a rate') +
  ggtitle(paste("My cool trees")) +
  theme(legend.position="right")

